SUMMARY:Disposable Humanity
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Ware Center for a free screening of the film Dis
 posable Humanity—plus a community discussion panel and a Q&A with the fi
 lmmakers. The Mitchell family—esteemed Disability Studies scholars and f
 ilmmakers—delve into the chilling legacy of the Nazi Aktion T4 program. 
 This investigative documentary recounts the long-obscured history of how o
 ver 300\,000 disabled individuals became the initial victims of the Third 
 Reich. Targeted by the T4 program as having a “life unworthy of living\,
 ” their murders laid the groundwork for the Holocaust that followed. 6:1
 5 PM • Pre-show community panel discussion Post-show • Q&A with direct
